  "definition": "An ergot alkaloid is a pharmacologic substance in the ergotamine group that can stimulate alpha-adrenergic receptors and narrow blood vessels. In the source material, this vessel-constricting action includes effects in arteries, veins, and cerebral blood vessels.",
